# Hui agent rules

- Read `ROADMAP.md` before starting a significant ticket; stay within the current ticket scope.
- Read relevant sections of `DECISIONS.md` and `docs/PRODUCT.md` before changing architecture or product behaviour.
- Do not re-paste the full product spec when repository docs already cover it.
- Keep changes bounded to the requested ticket; do not introduce dependencies without a clear reason.
- Prefer simple, maintainable implementations; keep domain rules out of UI components where practical.
- Treat privacy and authorisation as first-class: never rely on client-side checks alone; Supabase RLS must enforce data access.
- Write Vitest tests for important domain rules.
- Do not silently change established product decisions; flag ambiguous requirements that affect architecture or behaviour.
- At the end of every ticket, update `ROADMAP.md`, `WORKLOG.md`, and `TODO.md` only as needed—keep updates brief.
- Before declaring a ticket complete, run appropriate validation (`build`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` as configured).
- Commit completed work with a clear message and push to the current feature branch.
